    "q-170548": {
      "dom_id": "step-q170548",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Determine the points where the ellipse ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-6x+12y=7$ intercepts the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-6x+12y & =7 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(0)^{2}-6x+12(0) & =7 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =7 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x+9)-9 & =7 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{16} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-1,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(-1,0)$ and $(7,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-170548-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$(-3,0)$ and $(4,0)$",
