    "q-72915": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72915",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Determine the points where the ellipse ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-10x+8y+12=0$ intercepts the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the $y$-intercepts, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-10x+8y+12 & =0 \\\\ {0}^{2}+{y}^{2}-10(0)+8y+12 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}+8y+12 & =0 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-16+12 & =0 \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y+4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =-4\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =-6,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-6)$ and $(0,-2).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
